                                "sense_id": "ec718e41-47df-31c5-abff-cb2f9947aecb",
                                "text": "If there's a truly compelling reason not to normalize shaming as a global, always-on public spectator sport, it's not that it degrades the humanity of the shamed; it's not even the trite \"who among us has not canoodled at a Coldplay concert with his sidepiece\" justification. It's simply this: When we take joy in the distress and ruination of other people, we make monsters of ourselves."
